A||||6||Alex11||How much power can the stock tranny hold?||||1||
Z||000000||Alex11||06-15-2001||09:33 AM||||As the subject says, how much power can a stock tranny hold?  I f wanted to swap in a SB V8 with 500 horses, would it hold up?  If not, what tranny should I use?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tweek||06-15-2001||09:48 AM||||Though I dont know the answer to your question, it may help to say what year the car is, what motor came in it originally, and if it was an auto or manual, As there were several different trannys..<p>[This message has been edited by Tweek (edited 06-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||06-15-2001||10:14 AM||||I remeber seeing on v-8 archie's website that they installed 400 hp engines with stock transmissions and had no problems.  However if you're talking 500+ hp you might want to consult him.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex11||06-15-2001||10:18 AM||||Well I don't own a Fiero, so I don't know the specifics.  I am going to have a countach kit built for me, and would like it to have some balls but can't spend a fortune on said balls.  So I am just wondering how much power the thing can take with a standard V8 swap.  Does anyone know what the best manual transmission is for the fiero and which model year it came in.<P>Basically, what would be the best donor fiero for this application?||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||06-15-2001||10:26 AM||||I think Ive read 300Hp is most to safely use with stock trannies.||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||06-15-2001||11:04 AM||||they'll hold 500hp if you drive decent... if your a gear jammer and rail on the car at every light SOMTHING is gunna brake.. and it'll probly be the tranny case.. i think Tina had a similar failure... mine have held up to 300lbft (nitrous) with me driving like an idiot quite often... clutches on the other hand... tand to die.. stick with what ever archie recommends... he's the high priest of the V8 world||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tweek||06-15-2001||12:35 PM||||Found at Archies site:<P>Q. How much horsepower can the Fiero Stick shift transmissions handle? <P>A. Generally speaking I have used the following engine/transmission combinations with great success, in fact, I haven’t broke a stock Fiero stick shift transmission yet. <P>1) With the 4-speed trans. (‘84 4 cylinder & ‘85-’86 V-6 4 speeds) I have used 300+ H.P. engines repeatedly with no problems. <P>2) With the ‘85 thru ‘88 4 cylinder 5 speed transmissions I have used 300+ H.P. engines repeatedly with no problems. <P>3) With the ‘86 thru ‘88 6 cylinder 5 speed transmissions, I have used engines rated at 460+ H.P. (One even had an additional 200 H.P. dual quad carb. NOS system on top of a 460 H.P. 383" Chevy stroker engine) With no failures yet. <P>One final note on this subject: It is my opinion that: "even though we have had no failures, that any motor vehicle can fail if subjected to severe and constant abuse." <P>I just read through <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/faq.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/faq.htm</A>  Very informative||||reg||1
